{% comment %}
  Cellexia Reviews — app embed block (SPEC-1.5 §1).

  Enabled from the theme editor under Theme settings → App embeds — works on every
  theme, including themes that reject app blocks on product templates. When enabled:
  - product pages: emits a hidden widget shell (#cellexia-reviews-embed) that
    assets/cellexia-reviews.js relocates (placement_selector or heuristics),
    reveals per the SPEC-1.2 live/preview gating, and hydrates like the block.
    Blocks win: if the reviews app block is also on the page, the JS removes the
    embed root so nothing double-renders.
  - all pages: emits a #cx-embed-config JSON script the JS reads for the sitewide
    star-badge injector and the PDP title badge, plus the #cx-i18n dictionary
    (unconditional — the v1.10 §5A preview ribbon can mount on ANY tokenized
    not-live page, even with every widget/badge surface switched off, and must
    never render raw preview.* keys). v1.10 (SPEC-1.10 §1) adds
    pdp_badge_position (under_title — byte-identical default — or under_tagline)
    and pdp_badge_selector (advanced CSS-selector override), both carried in the
    config settings and honored by the title-badge code in the JS.

  Same live/preview gating as blocks/reviews.liquid (SPEC-1.2): the app-synced
  boolean SHOP metafield `cellexia.live` — only an explicit false means "not live";
  absent/invalid stays live (upgrade-neutral). The theme editor (request.design_mode)
  short-circuits the gating for the embed root exactly like the blocks, via
  data-cx-live. The root ships `hidden` ALWAYS — the JS un-hides it after placement
  when gating allows (live, preview token, or design mode).

  The assets are the same files the blocks load — the browser fetches them once.
  SSR content: none beyond the shell (JS renders everything; the config JSON carries
  rating/count for instant paint of the title badge). JSON-LD renders live-gated with
  a data-cx-jsonld="embed" marker so the JS can drop it when a block copy exists.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign cx_page_type = request.page_type
  assign cx_is_product = false
  if cx_page_type == 'product' and product
    assign cx_is_product = true
  endif

  comment
    v1.2 (SPEC-1.2): only an explicit false on the `cellexia.live` SHOP metafield
    means "not live" — absent/invalid values stay live so upgraded stores never
    go dark. The theme editor always allows the full widget (data-cx-live="true").
  endcomment
  assign cx_is_live = true
  if shop.metafields.cellexia.live.value == false
    assign cx_is_live = false
  endif
  assign cx_show_full = cx_is_live
  if request.design_mode
    assign cx_show_full = true
  endif

  comment
    v1.6 (SPEC-1.6 §3, RC-A): design-mode-only preview token, mirrored by the
    app into the SHOP metafield `cellexia.preview_token`. Emitted on the embed
    root AND inside #cx-embed-config (badge-only pages carry no root), but ONLY
    when request.design_mode is true — a normal storefront request must never
    contain a preview token anywhere in its HTML. Absent metafield ⇒ neither the
    attribute nor the JSON key is emitted.
  endcomment
  assign cx_editor_token = ''
  if request.design_mode
    assign cx_editor_token = shop.metafields.cellexia.preview_token.value | default: '' | append: '' | strip
  endif

  assign cx_lang = request.locale.iso_code | split: '-' | first

  assign cx_default_locale = 'en'
  for cx_loc in shop.published_locales
    if cx_loc.primary
      assign cx_default_locale = cx_loc.iso_code
    endif
  endfor

  assign cx_heading = 'cellexia.widget.title' | t

  comment
    App-synced shop metafields, nil-guarded exactly like blocks/reviews.liquid:
    brand display name (absent → JS falls back to "Cellexia") and translate
    buttons (only an explicit false disables).
  endcomment
  assign cx_brand = shop.metafields.cellexia.brand_display_name.value
  assign cx_show_translate = true
  if shop.metafields.cellexia.show_translate.value == false
    assign cx_show_translate = false
  endif

  comment
    v1.1/v1.3 design version: the case/when guards unknown or missing
    `cellexia.design_theme` values back to the default "amazon" skin —
    identical to blocks/reviews.liquid.
  endcomment
  assign cx_skin = 'amazon'
  case shop.metafields.cellexia.design_theme.value
    when 'cellexia'
      assign cx_skin = 'cellexia'
    when 'luxe'
      assign cx_skin = 'luxe'
  endcase

  comment
    Aggregate rating for the config JSON (instant title-badge paint) —
    metafield access nil-guarded exactly like blocks/reviews.liquid.
  endcomment
  assign cx_rating = 0
  assign cx_count = 0
  assign cx_dist = nil
  if cx_is_product
    assign cx_ns = product.metafields.cellexia
    if cx_ns.rating and cx_ns.rating_count
      assign cx_rating = cx_ns.rating.value | times: 1.0
      assign cx_count = cx_ns.rating_count.value | times: 1
    endif
    comment
      SPEC-1.12 §5: star distribution for the PDP badge's ratings-breakdown
      popover — instant SSR paint; absent metafield serializes as null and the
      JS falls back to the first widget list load (cellexia:loaded).
    endcomment
    if cx_ns.distribution
      assign cx_dist = cx_ns.distribution.value
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  v1.5.1 audit: the app-proxy base path is single-sourced in snippets/
  cx-proxy.liquid and carried in the config JSON too — badge-only pages
  (home, collections) have no widget root to read data-proxy from.

  v1.8 (SPEC-1.8 §5, MEASURED root cause): Shopify wraps every render of an
  app snippet in "BEGIN app snippet" / "END app snippet" HTML comments —
  including inside capture — so the captured value reached consumers as
  "<!-- BEGIN app snippet: cx-proxy -->/apps/…/api<!-- END app snippet -->",
  an invalid URL that broke the badge fetcher on every deployed page. Strip
  the exact wrapper strings after capturing; the filters are harmless when
  Shopify omits the comments. Both consumers below (the config JSON and the
  root's data-proxy attribute) read this cleaned variable.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture cx_proxy -%}{% render 'cx-proxy' %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign cx_proxy = cx_proxy | remove: '<!-- BEGIN app snippet: cx-proxy -->' | remove: '<!-- END app snippet -->' | strip -%}
{{ 'cellexia-reviews.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'cellexia-reviews.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script type="application/json" id="cx-embed-config">
{
  "pageType": {{ cx_page_type | json }},
  "proxy": {{ cx_proxy | json }},
  "settings": {
    "enable_product_widget": {{ block.settings.enable_product_widget | json }},
    "placement_selector": {{ block.settings.placement_selector | default: '' | json }},
    "enable_badges": {{ block.settings.enable_badges | json }},
    "badge_style": {{ block.settings.badge_style | default: 'stars_count' | json }},
    "badge_selector": {{ block.settings.badge_selector | default: '' | json }},
    "show_pdp_title_badge": {{ block.settings.show_pdp_title_badge | json }},
    "pdp_badge_position": {{ block.settings.pdp_badge_position | default: 'under_title' | json }},
    "pdp_badge_selector": {{ block.settings.pdp_badge_selector | default: '' | json }}
  },
  "skin": {{ cx_skin | json }},
  "live": {{ cx_is_live | json }},
  {%- if cx_editor_token != blank %}
  "editorToken": {{ cx_editor_token | json }},
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if cx_is_product %}
  "product": {
    "id": {{ product.id | json }},
    "handle": {{ product.handle | json }},
    "title": {{ product.title | json }},
    "url": {{ product.url | json }},
    "rating": {{ cx_rating | json }},
    "ratingCount": {{ cx_count | json }},
    "distribution": {{ cx_dist | json }}
  }
  {%- else %}
  "product": null
  {%- endif %}
}
</script>
{%- comment -%}
  v1.10 §5A: the i18n dictionary rides with the config script on EVERY page —
  previewBootstrap() mounts the preview ribbon on any tokenized not-live page,
  including pages where the widget, badges and PDP title badge are all disabled,
  and t() must find preview.* there. Small and cached. Shopify's app-snippet
  comment wrapper (SPEC-1.8 §5) lands OUTSIDE the emitted <script id="cx-i18n">
  tag, so getElementById is unaffected; a second #cx-i18n from a reviews block
  on the same page is harmless (getElementById takes the first, same content).
{%- endcomment -%}
{% render 'cx-i18n' %}
{%- if cx_is_product -%}
{%- if block.settings.enable_product_widget -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Hidden widget shell — same data-attribute contract as the reviews block root,
  but id="cellexia-reviews-embed" + data-cx-embed="true" and ALWAYS hidden.
  The JS relocates it (placement_selector or heuristics), reveals it per gating
  and builds every container itself (no SSR content in embed mode). The i18n
  dictionary is emitted unconditionally next to #cx-embed-config above.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  id="cellexia-reviews-embed"
  class="cx"
  {% if cx_lang == 'ar' %}dir="rtl"{% endif %}
  data-cx-embed="true"
  data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  data-product-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
  data-locale="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}"
  data-shop-default-locale="{{ cx_default_locale }}"
  data-proxy="{{ cx_proxy }}"
  data-per-page="10"
  data-heading="{{ cx_heading | escape }}"
  {% if cx_brand != blank %}data-brand="{{ cx_brand | escape }}"{% endif %}
  data-show-summary="true"
  data-show-media-strip="true"
  data-show-form="true"
  data-show-translate="{{ cx_show_translate }}"
  data-demo="false"
  data-cx-skin="{{ cx_skin }}"
  data-cx-live="{{ cx_show_full }}"
  {% if cx_editor_token != blank %}data-cx-editor-token="{{ cx_editor_token | escape }}"{% endif %}
  hidden
></div>
{%- endif -%}
{%- if cx_is_live -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Live-gated structured data. The marker makes the emitted script identifiable
  ([data-cx-jsonld="embed"]) so the JS removes it when a block copy exists —
  never two Product JSON-LD payloads from this app (SPEC-1.5 §3.6).
{%- endcomment -%}
{% render 'cx-jsonld', product: product, marker: 'embed' %}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:cellexia.embed_block.name",
  "target": "body",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enable_product_widget",
      "label": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.enable_product_widget.label",
      "info": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.enable_product_widget.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "placement_selector",
      "label": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.placement_selector.label",
      "info": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.placement_selector.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enable_badges",
      "label": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.enable_badges.label",
      "info": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.enable_badges.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "badge_style",
      "label": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.badge_style.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "stars_count",
          "label": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.badge_style.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "stars_only",
          "label": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.badge_style.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "stars_count"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "badge_selector",
      "label": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.badge_selector.label",
      "info": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.badge_selector.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_pdp_title_badge",
      "label": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.show_pdp_title_badge.label",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "pdp_badge_position",
      "label": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.pdp_badge_position.label",
      "info": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.pdp_badge_position.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "under_title",
          "label": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.pdp_badge_position.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "under_tagline",
          "label": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.pdp_badge_position.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "under_title"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "pdp_badge_selector",
      "label": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.pdp_badge_selector.label",
      "info": "t:cellexia.embed_block.settings.pdp_badge_selector.info"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
